# The sprite bundles ARE committed, and that is deliberate. They have to be
# served same-origin from GitHub Pages: release assets send no CORS headers at
# all, so a browser can never fetch() one, however convenient it would be to
# keep them out of the repo. Tested with an Origin header; there is no header
# to be had. Pages sends access-control-allow-origin: *.

# The loose per-species sprite packs are build INTERMEDIATES, not artefacts.
# They are what pack_bundle.py reads to build web/sprites-*.pak, and the .pak
# files are what actually gets distributed -- so tracking both puts the same
# ~105 MB of sprite data in the repo twice. Restore them with:
#
#   python3 tools/unpack_bundle.py       # from the committed .pak, no network
#
# or re-fetch from source, which is only needed when adding a region:
#
#   python3 tools/pack_pmd.py            # or: kanto / johto / hoenn / ...
#   python3 tools/make_thumbs.py
#
# YOU NEED THEM TO TAKE SCREENSHOTS. Without this directory the emulator draws
# every creature as a bare dex number, so tools/make_screens.sh would overwrite
# docs/screens/ with art-less images -- see CLAUDE.md § Screenshots.
#
# CREDITS.md recommends shipping the code and the scripts and letting each user
# package the sprites from the original sources, which is why the loose files
# stay out of the repo while the .pak bundles (which Pages must serve
# same-origin) stay in.
tools/sdcard/mons/*.bin

